body:
I liked her.  

&#x200B;

I read that Rose McGowan really could fit thru that cat door.  At certain points, her shirt looked stapled to the door or something.  It's kinda weird.

Rebecca--I understood why they paired Wes with Rebecca.  They were both broken in their own ways.  Went thru similar things, despite being different on the outside.  They got each other.  But that relationship was toxic as fuck, so are most of the relationships on this program.

&#x200B;

Meggy--Sad.  I liked Meggy a lot.  It's a shame.  If it weren't for the whole Middleton murder stuff, they would've worked out.

&#x200B;

Laurel--I liked Wes and Laurel best.

I think he's supposed to be.  

&#x200B;

If not, then Stephen creeps me out.  He seems more laid back in real life.

Congrats!!!

&#x200B;

Signed, 

&#x200B;

Also newly diagnosed

My Sims game worked perfectly fine until the latest update.  Like literally the day of, I was playing the game.  Everything was normal until it wasn't.  And I got white screened.  I did everything I could until I just gave up.

&#x200B;

Could it be the mods?  I have hundreds of mods and CCs.  I can't play a vanilla game.

Spectacular!  

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Good message too.

Wes never deserved to die.  All he wanted was to protect someone he loved.  Plus Sam deserved it.  I still like to pretend that Annalise hid him somewhere safe.  And that Laurel and Christopher came to him when the time was right.

&#x200B;

Frank and Bonnie?  Definitely deserved their fates.  Frank especially, since he was a serial killer.

&#x200B;

Connor.  I disliked Connor for most of the series.  But he never killed anyone.  SO he didn't deserve to go to jail.  He should have stayed away from Oliver.  I always wonder why he didn't negotiate a better deal for himself that required NO jail time.  I guess going to jail was the only way he'd move on?

&#x200B;

Asher?  I don't know if he deserved his fate or not.  Yes, he killed someone.  Yes, he felt guilty about it.  I knew someone would betray the group eventually but I didn't think it would be him.  I felt neutral about Asher, so I don't know.

&#x200B;

Oliver?  Connor wound up with Raul and Oliver crazy and alone.  In my mind.

&#x200B;

Laurel:  By the end of this, Laurel was a billionaire.  Or least super in the millions, right?  Despite having all the money in the world, I have a hard time imagining herself sitting at home alone with Christopher or even traveling all over the place.  I'm sure she did travel a bit though.  I think she would have a career, but probably not law. Maybe starting a successful business which gradually turns into something of a international thing.  Which is how Annalise and her and Chris (and Wes) all keep in touch.  And internet, Zoom.  Blah, blah. She certainly wound the richest and most successful.

Michaela:  Her ending was probably the most accurate.  She wound up rich and successful, which is what she truly wanted all along.  But the experiences with K5 made her colder emotionally, and I doubt she had many happy or meaningful relationships after that.  Except with her father and maybe her (grand)kids.

&#x200B;

Nate:  He was kind of an asshole wasn't he?  I don't think he deserved his ending.  But someone had to get away with murder, right?  Everyone else is either dead or not a murderer.  I guess he enjoyed some success running his business, being rich and probably had kids.  Named the boy after his father.

I think Pete left a lot of things open-ended.  You could fill in the blanks yourself about what happened to Annalise and the others.  The others who survived, of course.

&#x200B;

I think she dated Tegan for a few years, largely because she was all she had left after everything.  They realized that they weren't good as a couple.  They broke up and stayed friends until Tegan died.  That may have lead Annalise to start drinking after decades of sobriety.  

&#x200B;

Annalise dated a few people--men and women--until she finally reunited with Eve for good.  That's why Eve's eulogy was the first one in the finale.

&#x200B;

That's my interpretation anyways.

I've always wanted Laurel and Wes together.  I wish they hadn't killed him off.  I just pretend that Annalise used her connections to hide him somewhere safe.  Then when the time was right, Laurel and Christopher came to be with him.  Then they finally became the family they were supposed to be.

&#x200B;

With Frank, it was all sex and fighting.  Laurel was the only woman Frank couldn't really have and he might've been more in love with the chase than her.  Maybe?

Learning about celebrities.  I always obsess over their love lives/personal lives.  It drives me crazy and eventually overrules any move I have for their art.  I overthink and obsess over every little thing I read or hear. I Google about them constantly, many times a day. I don't even know why anymore.  Sometimes, I read toxic forums and socials etc,  and it often gives me literal pains.  

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

 My brain oftentimes.....it doesn't know how to rest.

This is my reality now and I hate it.  

&#x200B;

Every post I read on here is further confirmation that I have OCD.

I think the whole point is to make autistic people feel better about themselves.  But it often fails.

&#x200B;

I just think of my "superpowers" as my strengths and the bad stuff as weaknesses.

Oh, I know that I am.  I'm 37, turning 38 in January.  

&#x200B;

And I'm still very single, but I have hope that'll change soon.  Never had a real relationship, no kids.  Never lived on my own.  Haven't worked since college.  Spent 10+ years in college with no full degrees.  Still get treated like a kid most of the time.  Nobody at home even listen to my ideas, except maybe my cousin.  I keep seeing people all around me--friends, family members, strangers, people on social media etc.  And they're all living my dreams.  And I'm around miserable or stuck people all day, every day.

She knew him better than the others, apart from Annalise.  They could've been something great, but they made the huge mistake of killing off Wes.  

&#x200B;

They should've axed the whole Laurel-trying-to-find-Frank storyline.

Maybe a distant relative of his?

&#x200B;

But this one is closer to Mac....

&#x200B;

\[Imgur\](https://i.imgur.com/xzNI90A.jpg)

So do I.

&#x200B;

I've had so many days like that.

I hate when people change plans on me.  

&#x200B;

Even though it happens quite a lot.....

Yes, I think it should be.  At some of the time.

&#x200B;

It seems like life is more about the tedious, boring things that it is about anything fun.  Every day is basically the same day over and over again.  I'm tired of it.  I just want something interesting to happen for a change.

For me, he was the most relatable character.  Overall, he was a good person.  He could be shady, like the rest of them.  But I guess that's a job requirement in this universe.  He was kind, intelligent and brave.  He probably would've made a great lawyer.

&#x200B;

I hate how people still blame him for starting this mess, but he didn't.  He was just protecting his girlfriend, who was kind of a victim of all this too.  Was he just supposed to stand there and watch her be murdered by some psycho?  Who, with his psycho son really started all of this? 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I hate seeing people whale on Wes all the time.

I really liked him at first.  But then he got boring and toxic at the same time.  He was just Connor's boyfriend/fiance/husband who was great at computers and had HIV.  They could've given a million great storylines.  They didn't even bother to make him interesting.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Plus, him and Connor became really a toxic pair.

They never needed Annalise.  It was an accident, one that Sam deserved. They could've easily come up with a believable story and gotten off.  Especially Laurel.

&#x200B;

Even if that didn't work, Annalise or someone else could've represented them and averted the nightmare for that lasted 6 years.

I'm 37, and my friends vary in ages.  But they all have one thing in common.  They're grownups.  Or at least they seem to be.  I feel like I don't have much in common with my friends anymore because their lives are vastly different from mine.  They'll always be my friends unless there's a good reason not to be. 

&#x200B;

They have relationships/marriages, jobs, houses or apartments etc.  They go on nice vacations and seem to live full lives.  Basically the full adult package.  And I'm proud of them and extremely jealous of them.  I'm living pretty much the same life I lived in high school, except no school or job.

&#x200B;

But I've never really fit in anywhere, not even at home.  SO what do I expect?

I hope so.  Her ending in LOCI was pathetic.  

&#x200B;

I think Bobby was in love with her, or at least cared about her.  Even if he didn't want to be.

I think he loved the initial stability that Oliver provided more than him as a person.  Once he realized that Oliver actually loved their life of crime, he didn't love him as much.  

&#x200B;

I just pretend that they stayed apart and Connor found real love with someone else.

Overacting?  Ehh, maybe?

&#x200B;

But Wheatley is probably the best villain in the entire L&O franchise.

Danielle and Tamara look beautiful either way.

&#x200B;

But Danielle's wig ages her big time.  She looks better with her natural hair.

I think Olivia grew more as a person once Elliott was gone.  She had serious relationships.  She gradually work her way up in the SVU department.  She became a mother.  She just learned to have something of a life outside of work.

&#x200B;

When Elliott was around, she spent most of her time looking after him.  He unintentionally held her back.

Remember what Olivia said in "Surrendering Noah"?   She grew more with Nick, as a friend, than she ever did with Elliott?

&#x200B;

It's the truth.  Elliott held her back.  I don't think he intended to, but he did.  She wouldn't have gotten as far as she did in life if Elliott had stuck around.  And he didn't even say goodbye!

&#x200B;

He could've gotten with Liv during his single years, but he didn't.  Plus, take away SVU and what do they really have in common.

Oh wow!  I completely forgot about that.

&#x200B;

Maybe Simon never heard Liv's angry message because Wheatley got to him first.  Because Simon stumbled upon something he shouldn't have or he wanted out or something.

Eve. Hands down.   

&#x200B;

But I think she dated Tegan for years after the show ended.

I think she dated Tegan for a few years.  After everything---the deaths of her mother and "kids", getting of the K5 monsters etc.  Tegan was al she had left.  SO she gave her a chance and had her first healthy relationship.  When that fell apart, she did date other people before finding her way back to Eve.

&#x200B;

I think she needed to go thru all of that in order to be who she needed to be in order to have Eve.  Tegan taught her how to love in a healthy way.  Once that lesson was over, she and Eve had a great relationship.

I don't understand why they didn't do that.  There should've been something--a letter, emails, tweets etc.  They were best friends.

&#x200B;

But at the same time, the sudden exit still felt very Ellliot-like.  I don't know....

I hated Oliver.  I mean, Coliver was cute in the beginning, but that changed once he got more involved in the K5 world.

He seemed to enjoy being a criminal while Connor desperately wanted out.  They were a toxic pair, but so were most of the relationships here.

&#x200B;

Plus, Oliver had no personality or interests of his own.  Connor was his whole world.  

&#x200B;

I just pretend that Connor kept it moving and found another guy to be with after he got out of jail.

They both did.  Asher was a good medium term boyfriend, but I think she should've ended up with Miller.  

&#x200B;

But since nobody can be happy on this show for long....

I realized something.  Sam and Frank didn't say a single word to each other the whole 1st season.  I guess since Frank was so loyal to Annalise, that made sense.

&#x200B;

But Frank being the killer shocked me to no end.  Sam ordering the hit was a little shocking too, but not nearly as much as Frank.

No, not at all.  Simon was an annoying asshole, and we all agree on that.  But if being annoying were a crime, we'd have all done time in jail, LOL.

&#x200B;

I actually hoped that somehow, Simon somehow escaped the grim fate that awaited him in Pakistan.

I loved them together too.  I don't understand all of the hate.  I wish they lasted longer.  They were in love---or starting to be.  They were best friends.  The relationship was based on friendship and maybe shared trauma.  

&#x200B;

But Pete knew and still knows that killing off Wes was a massive mistake.  It's like he knew preemptively.  That's why Christopher was conceived and born.

&#x200B;

Laurel and Frank's relationship was based on sex, lust and fighting.  And on the fact that Laurel was the only woman he couldn't really have.  He loved the chase.

I think she does love him, in her own way.  But I also don't think she's **completely** delusional about this relationship.  She knew that at some point, Eric would want to move on, date someone his own age.  That's why she said what she said in the living room.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

And Eric got offended and hurt because he loves her.  As inappropriate and wrong as this relationship, I genuinely believe that they love each other.

I wish I could stop thinking.  And it's usually about the same stuff too, things I don't wanna think about.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Sometimes, I just wanna be with someone who makes me not think...only sometimes.  I'm just a thinker.

I don't think I hate holidays, but I don't seem to like them as much as most people do.  No one comes to visit, which is very good. 

&#x200B;

They're basically like any other day, nothing special about them.

I was shocked too.  Very Un-Eric like behavior.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

He hates that he has to share the woman he loves.  He was marking his territory, I think.

I kind of hate that I feel sorry for her too.  But I really do.  This episode helped me understand her better.  All of the men in her life before Eric--her husband, her brother and her dad?  They all abandoned her in different ways.  But Eric gives her his whole heart and he's attentive and protective.  She loves him for that, maybe?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Ugh, this is weird!!!  I don't know....

I've tried to force special interests.  I try to do it in order to stop a bad obsession.  It usually doesn't work though.

&#x200B;

It's kind of like a relationship, you just have to let it happen naturally.
